<h2 id="pocketbook-era-lite-launch">PocketBook Enters the 2026 E-Reader Race with the Era Lite</h2>

<p>PocketBook, one of Europe's largest e-reader manufacturers, has launched the <strong>PocketBook Era Lite</strong> in the United States market — a device that positions itself as the most compelling open-ecosystem alternative to Amazon's Kindle lineup. Available on Amazon for $199.99, the Era Lite brings together a 7-inch E Ink Carta 1300 display, physical page-turn buttons, and the company's trademark commitment to format freedom.</p>

<p>The Era Lite arrives at a pivotal moment for the e-reader market. Amazon recently ended support for 13 older Kindle models, triggering a wave of users looking for alternatives. Kobo continues to gain traction with its colour models and StoryGraph integration. But PocketBook's play is different: rather than competing on ecosystem lock-in, it competes on openness. The Era Lite supports 24 ebook formats out of the box — including EPUB, PDF, MOBI, FB2, DJVU, DOCX, RTF, and HTML — with no conversion required for most standard files.</p>

<p>This matters more in 2026 than it did five years ago. With Amazon's gradual shift toward DRM-free EPUB downloads and EPUB 3.3 becoming an ISO standard, the ebook world is converging on a single format. The Era Lite is designed to read that format natively, without the friction of Amazon's proprietary ecosystem or the conversion steps that Kindle ownership often demands.</p>

<h2 id="specs-and-design">PocketBook Era Lite: Specs and Design</h2>

