ly to the device. (3) Sideload directly — download EPUBs using the device's built-in browser and open them in the library.</p> </div> </div> </div> <div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"> <h3 itemprop="name">How does PocketBook Era Lite compare to Kindle Paperwhite?</h3> <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"> <div itemprop="text"> <p>The Era Lite offers native EPUB support and 24 format compatibility that the Kindle Paperwhite lacks. It includes physical page-turn buttons (Paperwhite has none). However, the Paperwhite has deeper IPX8 water resistance, lower starting price ($159.99 vs $199.99), and direct access to Amazon's Kindle Store and Kindle Unlimited. Choose the Era Lite for format freedom and button-based reading; choose the Paperwhite for Amazon ecosystem access and lower upfront cost.</p> </div> </div> </div> <div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"> <h3 itemprop="name">How much storage does the PocketBook Era Lite have?</h3> <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"> <div itemprop="text"> <p>The Era Lite comes with 16 GB of internal storage. For EPUB files, which typically range from 500 KB to 5 MB per book, this translates to roughly 3,000 to 10,000 books depending on file size and the presence of images. This is sufficient for the vast majority of readers, even those who maintain large reference libraries. PocketBook devices often support microSD expansion as well, although this was not confirmed at launch for the Era Lite.</p> </div> </div>
